            "title": "Spanish government cancels contract with Telefonica for using Huawei gear",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "MADRID (Reuters) -The Spanish government has cancelled a fibre-optic service contract with Telefonica over the use of equipment made by China's Huawei, the Digital Transformation Ministry said, amid concerns in Europe that such gear may pose a security risk.  The report by El Pais newspaper earlier on Friday also said  that through this 10 million-euro ($11.7 million) contract, Telefonica was to supply fibre-optic connections to a series of government institutions including the Defence Ministry.  Telefonica's Chief Operating Officer Emilio Gayo told Reuters last month that the company was \"reducing its exposure to Huawei\" in Spain to comply with EU recommendations to telecom operators to phase out Huawei-made devices over security concerns.",
